# Two-line hover help for desktop options
Workstream-ID: lea-19
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/19
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed desktop controls and fictional offline fixtures
Status: DONE
Milestone: Explain every desktop field and toggle at the point of use
Dependencies: lea-11, lea-14

## Purpose
Give each application-owned desktop field and toggle hover help containing
one purpose line and one practical-example line. Include changing action/tool
options, per-run settings, saved-search checkboxes, editor controls and tutorial
navigation. Keep the existing layout, CLI behavior and persistence unchanged.

## Tasks
- [x] Inventory fields, toggles, labels and action-dependent semantics.
- [x] Add consistent two-line native tooltips and useful label hover targets.
- [x] Exercise coverage, changing options and real tooltip display offline.
- [x] Review representative dark/light popups using fictional fixtures.
- [x] Update directly affected guides and visual references.
- [x] Independently verify the scoped issue, Project item and backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every application-owned input and toggle has a purpose and practical example.
- [x] Form labels and saved-search entries expose the corresponding help.
- [x] Changing actions/tools cannot leave misleading help on their fields.
- [x] Hovering does not start commands, create presets, save files or edit settings.
- [x] Native help remains readable in both existing themes and compact layouts.
- [x] Existing console diagnostics, settings, prior work and releases are preserved.
- [x] Offline evidence remains distinct from live qualification and human acceptance.

## Completion evidence
- A shared formatter supplies one purpose line and one Example line. Main
  window controls, all 24 dotted settings controls, labels, tabs, dropdown
  choices, saved searches, paths and tutorial navigation expose native help.
  Target/action and tool-input explanations update with their selected meaning.
- Five GUI suites passed 150 cases with native process exit zero. Scoped
  Black/Ruff passed seven changed Python files; GUI mypy passed nine source
  files. A tightened two-theme capture regression also passed with exit zero,
  checking that fictional path conversion cannot overwrite meaningful help.
- Actual native help events cover ordinary, internal, disabled and viewport
  targets. Checks preserve options, unsaved text, configuration bytes, private
  preset absence and an idle runner. Console diagnostic tooltips are retained.
- Captured and directly inspected dark/light native popup crops at expanded
  and compact sizes, plus the full expanded dark Limits still. Purpose and
  example remain readable on separate lines without clipping. Captures use
  owned offscreen widgets, temporary INI preferences and fictional workspaces;
  no shared desktop or independently running user window is captured.
- Refreshed the single affected README Limits PNG and eight directly affected
  guides. All fifteen GUI assets remain valid and all twenty-four retained
  README relative references resolve. Existing animations are unchanged.
  Documentation distinguishes current-source help from released v0.2.1 and
  accurately discloses the existing screenshot each-step flag limitation.
- Immutable-baseline comparison preserves 33 unrelated public files, all
  eighteen earlier tracking mappings, selected private size/mtime metadata,
  native preference registry metadata, HEAD and an empty staged diff.
  Private contents and preference values were not read for this comparison.
- Initial independent reconciliation verified the existing issue's exact
  managed content, one In Progress Project item and persistent backlink.
  Final completion settlement belongs in the index/ledger, outside this
  managed body, so its no-op rerun cannot create evidence churn.
- This is local source implementation and sampled offscreen rendering, not
  normal-desktop placement qualification, live automation, human aesthetic
  acceptance or publication. No user process restart, package build, commit,
  push, release replacement or tracking-service activation occurred.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-09: Started bounded two-line desktop hover help. Inspect actual
  run-option semantics and preserve the already-open user window, private
  inputs, prior console improvements and concise README curation.
- 2026-11-09: Implemented native purpose/example help across application-owned
  fields and changing options without modifying execution or persistence.
- 2026-11-09: Completed the 150-case GUI integration, tightened two-theme
  capture regression, direct popup review and affected documentation/media.
  Preserved earlier work and settings; the distributed executable is unchanged.
